Check out lines near 260 in allmain.c.  The dosounds()
routine and the invault() routines are called separately.
They are close together in the code, but they run
independently.

> Maybe the guard patrols the
> vault regularly and if he finds you in it, then he comes and talks
> to you?

In vault.c:

    if(++u.uinvault % 30 == 0 && !guard) { /* if time ok and no guard
now. */

So while you're in a vault (any vault in fact and the counter
can carry over) for 30 moves, the guard appears.

In sounds.c:

    if (level.flags.has_vault && !rn2(200)) {
        if (!(sroom = search_special(VAULT))) {
            /* strange ... */
            level.flags.has_vault = 0;
            return;
        }

The message has a 1-in-200 chance on a vault level.
You could hear footsteps whether you're in the vault
or not.  There are an assortment of other checks for
what happens if you're in the vault, if there's gold
in the vault and such.



